/* Veil Protocol content :: Chapter One scenes (opening + 5 roads). Authored module. */
Object.assign(window.VP.scenes, { opening:[
{img:"The mirror, 3:47am",t:["The internship ended on Friday. They shook your hand, said the usual things, and there is no office to go to now, no reason to be out before the light is. So you are home, the way you are always home these days, and the two rooms have learned the shape of one person in them a little too well.","You made dinner for two, out of a habit you have not had the heart to break. You ate your half standing at the counter and left his under an upturned plate, the way you do. You went to bed early, because the evening wanted nothing from you, and slept thinly, and woke at an hour with no name. In the kitchen the second plate was still cold under its cover, untouched. Gin had not come home.","You check the mirror the way you check the stove, and the lock, and the date on your phone. Twice. Some weeks ago once stopped being enough, around the time the city began to feel like a held breath, and you have told no one that and do not intend to.", "The face in the glass is yours. You make yourself confirm it the way you were taught to confirm anything that matters, slowly, almost out loud. Dark eyes a shade too awake. A jaw that is more Gin's than you like. Nineteen, though at this hour nineteen feels borrowed, a coat you are minding for someone. Rei. You think the name and the face agrees to it. Good. It keeps being your face, and you have learned to be grateful for the small, repeating mercies.", "Three forty-seven in the morning. The apartment has the particular quiet of a place where one person is awake and is no longer sure the other one is home. Outside, Kita-ku does the small honest work of being asleep. It does not know yet. Neither, quite, do you, but the knowing is already on its way up the stairs.", "Gin should be back by now. Gin is always back by now."],c:[{x:"Get up. Go and find him.",n:17}]},
{img:"The kitchen at this hour",t:["The kitchen is three steps and a whole different country at this hour. You fill the kettle out of habit and do not light it. Two cups sit upturned on the rack, because he insists on two, though he is never here for the second, and tonight the second cup is a small cruelty you set back down very carefully.", "Gin's keys are not on the hook.", "They have hung there every day since you were small enough to be lifted up to reach them. The brass is worn bright where his thumb always goes. The hook is empty now, and the bright worn place is only the shape of a habit with nothing left hanging in it. And Gin is late. Gin, who has not once in his life been late, who calls if he will be six minutes late, is late, and the keys are gone from the hook, and the kettle is going cold in your hand."],c:[{x:"Open the front door.",n:2}]},
{img:"The walkway, the cold key on the concrete",t:["You open the door before you have quite decided to. The walkway is empty. The sodium lamp buzzes the way it always buzzes. The city is exactly as large and as indifferent as it was an hour ago, and somehow that is the worst of it.", "The key is on the floor of the walkway, just past the threshold. Set down, or let fall, by a hand that did not come back for it. You crouch. It is cold the way only metal left out all night is cold, a cold that has finished arguing with the morning and lost.", "Left: a bicycle on its stand. A futon airing two doors down, exactly where it airs every fine day. Right: nothing. The street empty under the lamps, asleep, indifferent, perfect. Nothing else. That is the part that will not sit still in you afterward. How completely nothing else there is."],c:[{x:"Pick up the key and go back inside.",n:3}]},
{img:"Gin's field book, left on the table",t:["<p>Back inside, because inside is where answers are meant to keep. And there on the table, where it should not be, is Gin's archive... the book.</p>","<p>The field compendium... his archive, the thick soft-cornered thing he is never without... left out where you would find it, you understand later, addressed to whoever did, that he has carried into places you are not allowed to know about and carried out again. He did not take it. Wherever Gin went in the night, he went without the one object he does not leave behind.</p>"],c:[{x:"Pick up Gin's book.",n:4,do:'takeBook'}]},
{t:["<p>You put it in your bag. You put the cold key in your pocket, where it goes on being cold against your leg. And you let yourself think the sentence all the way to its end, the one you have held at arm's length since the empty hook:</p>","<p><em>Something has happened to Gin.</em></p>","<p>There. It is in the room now, and you cannot put it back. What you do next is yours, entirely... no one is making you chase this, no one would blame you for going to work and letting the proper people fail to find him. That is the worst of it, and the only freedom you have.</p>"],c:[{x:'Decide.',n:5}]},
{branch:true,t:["<p class='small'>Five roads lie under your hand like cards face-down. You will not get to walk them all. Choose the one most like you... or most like the person you would have to become.</p>","<p id='branchText'></p>"],c:[{x:"Open Gin's book and read his contacts.",n:11,need:'hasBook',hint:"His unregistered names... start where the records can't see.",do:'pathGrid'},{x:"Contact the CVD... ask for Okada.",n:12,need:'knowsOkada',hint:"The one name you have inside. Report him, be made theirs.",do:'pathCVD'},{x:"Contact Itsuki.",n:13,hint:"Your friend. Screens, records, someone awake at this hour.",do:'pathBuddy'},{x:"Reach for your gift... here, now.",n:14,hint:"Forbidden. It costs you. It might show you something.",do:'pathPower'},{x:"Just go out. Walk.",n:7,hint:"Let the city decide. The long way finds what the others miss.",do:'pathLook'},{x:"Read the scene like a trained operative.",n:6,lock:'clair3',hint:"Requires Clairsentience L3... you present as a low Sensitive (rank D). Reading a scene clean is past your disguise."}]},
{t:["<p>You have your first thread, and the morning has shown you what kind of story this is going to be.</p>","<p class='small'>[ End of the prologue. Five roads open from here... the Grid, the CVD, Itsuki and the Towers, the power you should not touch, and the long walk. They are being written. For now, you have found the one true thing: a man whose shadow falls the wrong way, at the Ōji overpass, the night Gin went quiet. ]</p>"],c:[{x:'↻ Start the morning over',n:0,do:'reset'}]},
{img:'Looking down the slope to Ōji',t:["<p>You leave the flat. The walkway, the long slope down to Ōji, wet concrete under sodium light, the sky still the flat black of the hours that have no name. You let your feet have the hour.</p>","<p>You could find the last ordinary place Gin stood... or keep walking until the city swallows the hour and the question with it.</p>"],c:[{x:'Walk to the Ōji overpass.',n:8},{x:"Tell yourself you'll forget it.",n:16}]},
{img:'The overpass... a cold spot where there should be none',ent:{name:'Residue... a Lingering',kind:'Minor entity · Class E · drawn to thin air',img:'Finding an entity',rows:[['Register','Fear'],['Threat','Low... confused, not yet hostile'],['Holds','A scrap of where it last felt safe'],['If exorcised','A tip... it saw a man with the wrong shadow'],['If absorbed','+Fear residue · Veil-thinness +']]},t:["<p>The Ōji overpass. You have crossed it a thousand times without thought. Tonight there is a cold patch in the middle of it... a column of air that does not belong to August... and under the traffic, almost nothing: a sound like a child trying not to cough.</p>","<p>Something is caught here. <em>Lingering.</em> It feels you notice it, and goes very still, the way small things go still when the large thing has finally looked their way.</p>"],c:[{x:'Reach out and read it.',n:9},{x:'Step around it and keep walking.',n:15}]},
{t:["<p>As it comes apart... sent back, or simply spent... it leaves you the one thing it had been holding, the way a hand opens after.</p>","<p><em>A man crossed this overpass the night Gin stopped answering. The Lingering watched him pass, and his shadow fell the wrong way: ahead of him, against the light, as though something walked a half-second behind the man it belonged to.</em></p>","<p class='small'>You write it down. Your first true thread: <b>a man with the wrong shadow... Ōji overpass, the night Gin vanished.</b></p>"],c:[{x:'Follow the thread.',n:10}]},
{t:["<p>The thread points two ways at once: <em>who</em> walks with a shadow that arrives before he does... and <em>where</em>, in Gin's own files, that man might already be named.</p>","<p>Whatever road you chose to get here, it has brought you to the same cold middle of the same bridge. That is either fate or a small mercy, and you are too tired this morning to tell them apart.</p>"],c:[{x:"Just go out. Walk, and let the city find you.",scene:'look',n:0,showIf:'look',do:'beginLook',hint:"No ally, no power, no institution. Only attention."},{x:"Reach for the gift you should not touch.",scene:'power',n:0,showIf:'power',do:'beginPower',hint:"No ally, no institution. Only you, and what you have hidden."},{x:"Take the thread to the Grid.",scene:'grid',n:0,showIf:'grid',do:'beginGrid',hint:"Gin’s book holds the names not in any record."},{x:"Take the thread to the CVD.",scene:'cvd',n:0,showIf:'cvd',do:'beginCVD',hint:"Okada is the one name you have inside."},{x:'Take the thread to Itsuki... begin Chapter One.',scene:'itsuki',n:0,showIf:'buddy',do:'beginItsuki',hint:'Your oldest friend. A Kuroda, of the Tower house.'},{x:'Begin your road →',n:6},{x:'↻ Start the morning over',n:0,do:'reset'}]},
{t:["<p>You open the book to the back, past the official pages, to where Gin keeps the names that are in no record... the Grid, written small. One is pressed twice, the way he underlines a thing that matters: <em>Tanizaki.</em> His thread is open on your phone now; talk to him, prove who you are, and he may point the way.</p>","<p class='small'>And whatever he tells you, the morning is already pulling you one direction: down the long slope to the Ōji overpass, where Gin was last ordinary. <span style='color:var(--dim)'>(Keep texting him... his thread is on your phone.)</span></p>"],c:[{x:'Go to the Ōji overpass.',n:8}]},
{t:["<p>Okada is the only name you have on the inside. Her thread is open on your phone... push her, carefully, and she may tell you more than the files allow.</p>","<p class='small'>Either way the morning is pulling you one direction: down to the Ōji overpass, where Gin last stood. <span style='color:var(--dim)'>(Keep texting her... her thread is on your phone.)</span></p>"],c:[{x:'Go to the Ōji overpass.',n:8}]},
{t:["<p>Itsuki’s thread is open on your phone... your oldest friend, awake at the worst hour, already worried about Gin too. Tell him what you need; he’ll find it.</p>","<p class='small'>And you both already know where tonight starts: the long slope down to the Ōji overpass, where Gin was last ordinary. <span style='color:var(--dim)'>(Keep texting him... his thread is on your phone.)</span></p>"],c:[{x:'Go to the Ōji overpass.',n:8}]},
{img:'Reaching for the gift you should not touch',t:["<p>You reach for the thing you are not supposed to do. The room tilts; the light goes thin and wrong, like water seen from underneath.</p>","<p>For half a second you are somewhere else: cold concrete, traffic overhead, the smell of a river that is not quite a river. A shape passes, and its shadow goes the wrong way... ahead of it, against the light. Then your own kitchen slams back around you and your skull is a struck bell. <span class='small'>(−12 Stability.)</span></p>","<p class='small'>You know the place. The Ōji overpass.</p>"],c:[{x:'Follow the vision.',n:8}]},
{t:["<p>You step around it and keep walking. Three steps on, the cold comes with you... it has caught on <em>you</em> now, not the bridge, a small persistent ache behind the sternum like a name you cannot place.</p>","<p>There is no walking away from this one. There rarely is, you suspect. That is going to be the shape of the whole thing.</p>"],c:[{x:'Turn and face it.',n:9}]},
{t:["<p>You tell yourself you will forget it... go back to bed, be a person to whom nothing has happened. Your feet take you down the slope toward Ōji anyway. They always know before you do.</p>"],c:[{x:'Let them.',n:8}]},
{img:"The flat at 3:47, one lamp on",t:["Two rooms and a kitchen the size of an apology, and you have lived here long enough to walk it blind. You do not walk it blind tonight. You put the lamp on, which you never do, because the dark has lately started to feel like it is paying attention.", "His door. The genkan, where the shoes are kept. His phone, which he answers on the second ring, always, even asleep, even angry. The kitchen, where the keys live on their hook. You could start anywhere. You notice that you are choosing the order the way you choose things at work, as if it will matter later which one you checked first."],c:[{x:"Look in Gin's room.",n:18},{x:"Check the genkan and the bathroom.",n:19},{x:"Call Gin's phone.",n:20},{x:"Go to the kitchen.",n:1,hint:"Where the keys hang."}]},
{t:["Gin's room is made up the way a soldier makes a bed, which he never was, and the squared corners accuse you of something you cannot name. The desk is too tidy. The chair is pushed all the way in. On the shelf, the spine of a notebook you have watched him write in and then close fast whenever you came near.", "He is not here. Of course he is not here; you would have heard him. But the room has a particular absence to it, a sense of having been left rather than simply being empty, and you cannot tell if that is true or if you are doing the thing you were warned about, finding shapes in the quiet because the quiet frightens you.", "A photograph is propped against the base of the lamp. The two of you, years ago, squinting into the sun. He keeps it where he can see it from the bed."],c:[{x:"Take the photograph, and step back.",n:17,item:{n:"A photo of you and Gin",e:"🖼",img:"Rei_Gin_Together",d:"The two of you years ago, squinting into the sun. He kept it where he could see it from the bed."}},{x:"Back to the hall.",n:17},{x:"Go to the kitchen.",n:1}]},
{t:["The genkan first. His work shoes are gone, which means nothing, he wears them everywhere; his good shoes are here, which means nothing either. You crouch and study the row of them the way you would study a scene, and hate yourself a little for it. There is no story in a row of shoes. You build one anyway, and then make yourself take it apart.", "The bathroom. His toothbrush, dry. A towel folded with the small carefulness he brings to the things he does not think about. The mirror in here is the one you do not check twice. You keep your eyes off your own reflection and do not look too closely at why."],c:[{x:"Back to the hall.",n:17},{x:"Go to the kitchen.",n:1}]},
{t:["You call him. You have called him a thousand times; your thumb finds the name without your eyes. It rings once, which is already wrong, because Gin answers on the second ring or not at all, and there is no version of tonight in which he lets your call ring through.", "It rings a second time. A third. Then his voice, flat and recorded and a year out of date, telling you to leave a message; the cheerful little tone; and the silence afterward that is yours to fill. You do not fill it. You end the call and stand there holding a phone that has become, very suddenly, just a phone."],c:[{x:"Back to the hall.",n:17},{x:"Go to the kitchen.",n:1,hint:"The keys."}]}
],
itsuki:[
{img:"Itsuki’s studio at Geidai, before the cleaners",t:["Geidai, before the cleaners come. Itsuki’s studio smells of linseed oil and cold convenience-store coffee, and every third canvas is the same bridge, the Ōji overpass, painted and repainted, each one wrong in a way he cannot name and will not sell.", "You tell him about the cold spot, and the shadow that fell the wrong way. He stops cleaning the brush. For a Kuroda, even a blocked one, a wrong shadow is not a turn of phrase; it is a second presence, possessed or accompanied, and he has grown up knowing the difference. “That’s why they keep coming out wrong,” he says, to the canvases. “I’ve been painting something that was already there.” He sets the brush down. “Tell me what you need. I was in the second you said his name.”"],c:[{x:"Let him in. Tell him everything.",n:1,do:'itsukiCommit'}]},
{t:["There are two ways a Kuroda gets you somewhere fast, and they are not the same kind of danger. One: the family. Real teleportation, Sei’s reach, the oldest house in the city, and a grievance older than your morning that the family will make you both pay to cross. Two: Itsuki’s own gift, which never opened clean, so he goes through paintings instead, a forgery of the real thing that costs him more each time and has never once landed exactly where he aimed it.", "“The family is safer for me and worse for you,” he says, turning the dead brush over. “They help, eventually, expensively, and they want to know everything, and a Kuroda knowing your business is its own kind of debt. The painting is worse for me and faster for you. It hurts, and it lands where it wants, not where I point.” He will not choose for you. “Your brother. Your call.”"],c:[{x:"Go to the family. Ask Kuroda Sei.",n:2,hint:"Safer, slower; the Kuroda never forget what you owe them."},{x:"Let Itsuki try the painting.",n:8,hint:"Faster, it costs him, and it does not land where he aims."}]},
{img:"The Kuroda compound, Nezu",t:["Nezu, where the city keeps its oldest money and its oldest quiet. The Kuroda compound does not announce itself; the most isolated house in Tokyo has no need to. Old wood, a wall that has outlived three governments, a stillness that is not peace so much as attention.", "A cousin meets you at the gate. Not Itsuki’s ally. She has his cheekbones and none of his softness, and she is the real thing, a teleportist who can read the air you displaced getting here. “You brought an outsider,” she says to him, and to you she says nothing, and her hand does not leave the doorframe, where a sigil you can almost see is cut into the wood: a ward keyed to her, a door she could close on you in a way that does not involve the door."],c:[{x:"Ask, plainly, for the family’s help.",n:3,do:'towerGate'}]},
{t:["The family will not be hurried and cannot be charmed. What stands between you and Sei is older than your morning: the blocked gift, a debt, a name Itsuki is not supposed to use as leverage. But there is a worse thing in the room, and you feel the cousin decide whether to say it. She says it. “A wrong shadow carrying weight. You are describing a seated one.” She means the Thirteen, the thirteen demons of the thirteen emotions, and the drop in her voice tells you the Kuroda have skin in that game older than the CVD, older than the wards.", "Itsuki goes pale. “If you make me spend the name to get Sei’s reach,” he says, low, “I do not get it back, and the family will own that I spent it, and on what.” The cousin watches you both, waiting to see how much you will cost him."],c:[{x:"Spend it. Make the family help, whatever Itsuki owes after.",n:4,do:'towerPress'},{x:"Find another way in. Don’t bleed him for it.",n:4,do:'towerSpare'}]},
{img:"Kuroda Sei, and the family’s anchor-stone",t:["Kuroda Sei receives you the way deep water receives a stone. Singular among them for control, younger than you expected, stiller than anyone alive, and he has already decided three things you will not be told. On the low table sits the family’s anchor: a teleport-stone the colour of a bruise, the artifact the Kuroda reach through, old enough that the lacquer has gone to glass.", "The cousin makes her move while he weighs you. A Tower rival’s gambit: she sets her own working against the room, a binding meant to make you not worth the family’s risk, and the air goes thick and wrong and for a moment you cannot say your own brother’s name. Sei stops it with a glance, not kindly, the way one stops a child. “A wrong shadow at Ōji,” he says into the silence he made. “The night a Directorate officer stopped answering.” Not a question. The case has caught on him, on the family, for reasons that are theirs. “I will reach once. Toward the man, not the brother. Hold the stone, and do not be stupid in the half-second you are nowhere.”"],c:[{x:"Take the stone. Take Sei’s reach.",n:5,do:'seiOpens'}]},
{t:["The world folds and does not hurt, which is its own kind of wrong, and for half a heartbeat you are nowhere, a place where here and there are the same word. Then a damp underpass assembles around you, the river that is not quite a river close by, and the place still remembers the man.", "What the Kuroda reach hands you is the family’s kind of knowledge, the cosmological kind. The thing the man carried is a seated one, top-grade, of the DUTY register, and the Towers have spent generations afraid of exactly this: a seat of the Thirteen on the move, looking. Sei’s voice reaches you across the fold, flat. “We do not go near a seated one. Find your brother, intern. But do not bring it to our door.”"],c:[{x:"Read the rest the family left.",n:6}]},
{t:["There is more here, in the way the whole house flinched, and you can take it or leave it. To see it you would have to read the compound the way Sei read you, past your own careful disguise, the thing you never do in front of anyone."],c:[{x:"Read what the Kuroda are truly afraid of.",lock:'clair3',n:7,do:'towerSecret'},{x:"Don’t. You have what you came for.",n:7,do:'towerLead'}]},
{t:["You surface owing the oldest house in the city a debt with no number on it, and Itsuki owing it more, and the half-degree the world now sits off true from standing where no one should stand. You have the family’s truth: the man carries a seat of the Thirteen, DUTY, and the Towers will not follow it, and that fear is older than anything the CVD would admit to.", "[ End of Chapter One, the Tower way. You hold the cosmological edge: a seated demon of DUTY on the move, and a lineage that has feared this longer than the wards have existed. What it is to the man, and to your brother, is the half you did not buy. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]},
{img:"Itsuki cuts his palm for ink and opens the canvas",t:["Back in the studio, Itsuki turns the worst canvas to face the room, the Ōji overpass at dusk, the one he could never finish, and you finally see the shape he has been almost-painting and scraping out for weeks: a figure on the bridge, its shadow thrown forward, into the light it should have been falling away from.", "“I can make it a door,” he says. “I can’t make it a safe one, and I’ve never carried someone.” He cuts his palm, not for drama, for ink, and presses the blood-and-linseed flat to the wet paint, and the studio thins around you like breath on glass, and the smell of oil becomes the smell of the river, and you go through."],c:[{x:"Go through with him.",n:9,do:'paintingJump'}]},
{t:["You come out wrong. Not the overpass. The painting took you where the painting wanted, the way Itsuki swore it might, to the thin place at the edge of the thing it had been trying to show him, and you stand in a low warded hall that smells of incense and river-water, faint shapes massed in the rafters, and you understand a second too late that you have arrived inside the reach of something that gathers.", "Itsuki is bleeding from the nose and will not say how much that crossing took. “A congregation,” he breathes, naming it the way his family taught him to name dangers. “A cult-kept place. Rei, the painting brought us to the grief, because the grief is where your man crossed.” The Far-Shore Circle. Higan-kai. The place the taken are recruited, not seized. Drawn down."],c:[{x:"Hold still and read the hall.",n:10}]},
{img:"A working medium mid-rite, a person ridden rising",ent:{name:"A person ridden",kind:"Far-Shore recruit, half given over · Register Grief",img:"Borrowed sorrow worn like a coat",rows:[["Register", "Grief"], ["Truth", "A grieving recruit, drawn down not seized"], ["The enemy", "is the rite, not the woman"], ["Free her", "reach past the sorrow, do not strike the body"]]},t:["A working medium of the Circle is mid-rite at the far end, and she has felt you arrive the way a spider feels a thread, and she does not stop her working; she turns it. A woman near her, a grieving recruit already half given over, a person ridden, rises and comes for you wearing borrowed sorrow like a coat, and the medium’s voice follows it, patient. “You came to the right place. Everyone here came to put a grief down. You could put yours down too.”", "You have salt in one pocket and the cold key your brother dropped in the other, and Itsuki at your back with a gift already spent. The ridden woman is the one in danger, not the enemy; the enemy is the rite. You will have to break it without breaking her, with what you brought."],c:[{x:"Ground on Gin’s key and free her; don’t fight the body.",n:11,do:'cultFight'},{x:"Grab Itsuki and run for the tear before it closes.",n:13,do:'paintFlee'}]},
{t:["It comes loose all at once, the borrowed grief, and the woman folds down around her own again, which is hers, and survivable, which is more than the rite offered her. The medium does not chase; she watches you leave with the patience of one who knows the grieving always come back. In the space the rite leaves you get what the place was holding.", "The man with the wrong shadow came here, to the grief, the same as the woman, and he was not seized. He walked in carrying a sorrow the Circle could not feed on, because it was already feeding something else, a passenger of the DUTY register, and he walked out north, toward water, unafraid, and the Circle is afraid of him the way small predators fear a large one passing through."],c:[{x:"Take it and get out.",n:12}]},
{t:["You get out the hard way, through a tear that is closing, and it takes the last of what Itsuki had. On the other side, in his studio, he sits down on the floor and does not get up for a while, and when he tries to tell you it is fine, you see what the crossing cost: the painted overpass on the easel is blank now, scraped clean by nothing you did, and when Itsuki reaches for it, he cannot make the colour come.", "“It’ll come back,” he says, not certain, the first uncertain thing you have ever heard him say. You did not pay the price for this road. He did, and he would do it again, and that is the worst of it."],c:[{x:"Sit with him a while, then go.",n:13,do:'paintLead'}]},
{t:["You come back to the morning owing a debt you cannot repay, because it is not yours; it is Itsuki’s, spent on you, in a currency he may not get to earn again. You have the human-and-occult truth: a cult that recruits the grieving, a man who walked through it carrying DUTY and out the other side unafraid, north, toward water. And a cult that has your face now, and your friend’s.", "[ End of Chapter One, the painting’s way. You hold the close, costly edge: the grief the man crossed, the Circle that fears him, the price your oldest friend paid to put you there. What the great houses know of a seated demon stays past a door you chose not to knock on. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]}
],
cvd:[
{img:"CVD HQ, Marunouchi... two ways to find anything out",t:["The Civil Veil Directorate keeps its real work behind a tower in Marunouchi that looks like every other glass tower on the block, which is the point. Okada is waiting in the lobby, because you do not get past the lobby. Terse, buttoned, a woman who keeps the files honest and resents being made to stand in a public space to do it. “You came in person,” she says, not pleased. “I told you to call the number.”", "You tell her anyway. The key. The cold. The shadow that fell ahead of the man it belonged to. Something moves behind her eyes and is filed away before you can read it. Then she says: “There are two ways a person finds anything out in this building, and they do not lead to the same place. Choose carefully. You only get to be new here once.”"],c:[{x:"Ask how it works.",n:1}]},
{t:["She lays it out the way she lays out a file, flat and complete. “One. You report him, on the record, and the Directorate opens a door for you and a file on you in the same motion. You get the system. The system gets you, and does not give you back. What is in the official record is yours; what is sealed in it is not; and a great deal is sealed.”", "“Two. I look for you. Off the books, off my own login, on my own neck. No file with your name on it. But you get what I can carry out in my head and my mouth, the human shape of it, the part no form holds, and you do not get the record, because the record is the thing I would be risking everything to even glance at.” She waits. “They are not the same truth, and you do not get both. Not as a stranger. So. Which half of your brother do you want?”"],c:[{x:"The record. Report him officially.",n:2,hint:"The institution’s truth. You become theirs to get it."},{x:"The human truth. Let Okada look off the books.",n:7,hint:"What no file holds. She risks herself; the record stays dark to you."}]},
{t:["You sign. A form for being someone’s brother, a longer one for what you saw, a longer one still for consenting to be assessed as next of kin. They take your name, your level as they read it (a D, a nobody, which is what you have always let them think), your address, and enter all of it into Component One, the Catalogue, where it will sit and be readable for the rest of your life. The door opens and closes behind you in the same motion. You are theirs now, a little. That was the price on the form."],c:[{x:"Let them assess you.",n:3,do:'cvdRegister'}]},
{t:["The assessor is pleasant the way a scale is pleasant. A few questions. A card with a symbol you are told not to think about, then asked what you thought about. The standard battery for a low Sensitive. Near the end she pauses, the smallest pause, makes a note you are not shown, and says “Unremarkable,” which is the word you wanted. The pause is the word you did not.", "You could let it pass, the way you have let everything pass your whole careful life. Or you could do the thing you never do in front of them: read her back, the way she is reading you, and see what the pause was hiding."],c:[{x:"Read the assessor as she reads you.",lock:'clair3',n:4,do:'cvdSecret'},{x:"Stay unremarkable. Let it pass.",n:4}]},
{t:["With your name in the system, Okada lays the file in front of you, and you see how much of it is the shape of what is missing. You take the pieces it will give. A time: the overpass, logged at 1:14 in the morning, the exact minute a thread on your phone says Gin stopped answering. A note in the dry CVD hand: SECOND-PRESENCE INDICATORS, SUBJECT UNCOOPERATIVE. And a clearance stamp on the seal, an office, not a name, but an office high enough that Okada goes very still when she sees whose it is.", "“That is the record’s edge for me,” she says. “Past it, grey, sealed, stamped by someone who could end me for showing you even this.” There is, she does not quite say, a floor below this one, where the things behind the seal are kept."],c:[{x:"Push. Ask to see the floor below.",n:5,hint:"The asset shelf. It costs, and it is on no tour."},{x:"Take the pieces you have and go.",n:6,do:'cvdRegLead'}]},
{img:"The floor the lobby never mentions",ent:{name:"A contained asset",kind:"Behind ward-glass · Register Grief · CVD inventory",img:"Rows of containment, a faint shape in each",rows:[["Register", "Grief"], ["Truth", "Something kept at work; logged the same night"], ["Holds", "the one piece the file would not: where he went"], ["Cost", "the cold stays in you a while"]]},t:["Okada should not, and does, walk you past a door the lobby never mentions, down to where the Directorate keeps what it takes. Rows of containment, each tagged with a designation number, a faint shape in every one. Souls kept as inventory. No one here calls it that. One of them was logged the same night your man crossed, and it presses to the ward-glass when it feels you notice it, and it holds the one piece the file did not: where he went."],c:[{x:"Reach past the glass and take the piece it holds.",n:6,do:'cvdAsset'},{x:"Don’t. You have enough to carry out.",n:6,do:'cvdRegLead'}]},
{t:["You walk out of Marunouchi with the institution’s shape of your brother in your hands and a weight in your chest that is not the cold. A time. A tell. The stamp of an office high enough to frighten the one honest person inside. You know the Directorate knows what took the man on the bridge, and has decided, from a height, that you are not to. You do not know what your brother became. That is the half you traded away, and the system you traded it for has your name now, and your level, and your address.", "[ End of Chapter One, the Directorate’s way. You hold the record’s edge: a sealed case, a logged minute, a clearance that scared Okada silent. What the seal hides, and where the man went, lie past a door you are now inside of, and watched within. To learn the human why, you would have to ask the people who loved him, off any record at all. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]},
{img:"Two coffees, two streets over, off any record",t:["She does not take you inside. She takes you to a vending-machine corner two streets over, buys two coffees, drinks neither. “Off the books means off the books,” she says. “If this comes back, it comes back on me, not the file, because there will be no file. What I give you, I give with my own neck, and only because your brother was the kind of man you do this for.”", "That is the most she has ever said about him, and she says the rest looking at the coffee. “The last weeks, he was wrong. Not sick. Wrong, the way a room is wrong after something has stood in it. And he was protecting something. Carefully. Quietly. I think,” she says, and stops, and you understand she has decided to be honest, “I think he was protecting you.”"],c:[{x:"Ask what he was protecting you from.",n:8,do:'cvdOff'}]},
{t:["She does not know from what. That part is sealed even from her. But she knows where: in the last weeks, Gin kept going north, to the water, to a stretch of riverbank he had no case in and no reason for, again and again, at hours when the cameras are out. “He never logged it,” she says. “A man does not log the place he goes to do the thing he is hiding. I only know because reading the gaps in what people log is my whole job, and his gaps all pointed the same way.”", "North. The water. The same direction the man on the bridge was walking. You feel the two facts touch in your chest, and you do not yet let yourself say what shape they make together."],c:[{x:"Follow where he kept going.",n:9}]},
{img:"A stretch of riverbank with no reason in it",ent:{name:"A witness the water keeps",kind:"Caught at a doorway · Register Grief · not the tower’s",img:"A residue at the waterline",rows:[["Register", "Grief"], ["Truth", "Left behind where Gin came in secret"], ["Remembers", "the last night, when he did not come alone"], ["Be gentle", "it is not the tower’s to take"]]},t:["You go where his gaps pointed, to a stretch of riverbank with no reason in it, and the reason is waiting. Not the man. Something smaller, left behind, a residue caught at a doorway the way grief catches: a witness, not the Directorate’s kind, the kind the water keeps. It was here for the thing Gin came to do, over and over, and it remembers him, and it remembers the last night he came, not alone."],c:[{x:"Reach for what it remembers of him.",n:10,do:'cvdWitness'},{x:"You aren’t ready for the last night. Step back.",n:10,do:'cvdOffLead'}]},
{t:["You walk back up from the water with the human shape of your brother in your hands and no proof of any of it. You know he changed. You know he was protecting you, from a thing he would not name. You know he came here, north, to the water, to do something in secret, and that on the last night he did not come alone. You understand him, which is the half you chose. You do not have the record, the seal, the office, the proof, the name of whoever in that glass tower decided he was a thing to be hidden rather than a man to be found.", "[ End of Chapter One, the quiet way. You hold the human edge: a brother who changed, who was protecting you, who went north to the water in secret and did not come back from the last night alone. What the Directorate logged and sealed stays dark to you. To hold that, you would have to become theirs. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]}
],
grid:[
{img:"Sanya... the door to the Grid",t:["Minami-Senju, the end of a train line most maps treat as the edge of the world. Tanizaki’s door is a back room behind a back room, in Sanya, where the city keeps the people it would rather forget. No sign. A kettle. He does not look up. He pours tea, pours a second cup and slides it across without being asked, and you understand there is a ritual here you are already failing.", "“Gin’s brother,” he says, not a question. “The intern. He talked about you for years. Never once brought you here.” He listens to the key, the cold, the shadow that fell ahead of the man, the way deep water listens. “I do not exist on paper. Neither does the help you want. So before I spend any of it, understand how we work, and what it costs.”"],c:[{x:"Ask the Grid for help.",n:1}]},
{t:["The Grid is the opposite of the tower. No files, no catalogue, no protection, no standing you have not earned, no one who must help you because a form says so. The unregistered survive by being unfindable and by owing one another carefully. A favor here is a real thing, with weight, and never free.", "“Two ways,” Tanizaki says. “You spend something your brother left you. He had credit with me, a name, and you are his blood; that opens a door, once. Or you earn your own, by doing the Grid a turn before it does you one. They are different doors, and they open on different rooms. Gin would tell you to earn it. Gin is not here.”"],c:[{x:"Spend Gin’s credit. Use his name.",n:2,hint:"Opens the inner door. The Grid never forgets a debt."},{x:"Earn your own. Do the Grid a turn first.",n:8,hint:"Action, and a chance to lose, and standing that is truly yours."}]},
{img:"The Gathering, and the Switch at the door",t:["You say your brother’s name like a key and it turns. Tanizaki takes you to the Gathering, which is less a place than an agreement about one; the Switch moves it, scrubs it from the kind of attention that finds things, and you arrive without quite knowing how, into a warded room above a coin laundry, ward-marks on every wall drawn by hands that meant them.", "You are there a minute before it goes wrong. The Switch, a wire-thin woman who keeps the Grid invisible, comes off the wall white-faced. “Sweep,” she says, one word, and the room moves like a kicked nest. A Directorate sweep, inbound, because the man’s passage has left the whole ward thin and ringing and the tower is hunting the disturbance and does not care whose door it opens to find it. The unregistered are about to be very findable."],c:[{x:"Help. Don’t be the reason they get caught.",n:3,do:'gridScatter'},{x:"Grab Tanizaki. Get your answer before this scatters.",n:3,do:'gridGrab'}]},
{t:["You make your choice in the half-minute the city gives you, and the Gathering comes apart around it the way the Grid has survived a hundred sweeps: not in panic, in practice, every person a door to somewhere else, the room emptying into the laundry steam and the back alleys and the cracks the tower’s map does not have.", "Tanizaki holds you back a beat in the emptying room. “You want what the man left in the ward,” he says. “We keep someone who can read that. Come. Quietly. And whatever she shows you, you did not see it here, because after tonight there is no here.”"],c:[{x:"Go to the one who reads the dead.",n:4,do:'gridName'}]},
{t:["She is old in a way that has nothing to do with years, a Grid sensitive who reads the residue the dead leave the way other people read a room, and she has been refusing to sleep for a week. “Your man,” she says, before you ask. “He has been crossing the ward going north for a month, and he changed on the way. I have watched it happen in the marks he leaves.”", "She tells you the part the Grid has been too frightened to log: the Far-Shore Circle, the Higan-kai, the cult that feeds on grief, has been gathering hard along his path, and the man passed straight through their reach and they did not take him, because he was already taken, by something the Circle is afraid of. “Whatever rides him,” she says, “the predators get out of its way.”"],c:[{x:"Ask her to read the weight of it.",n:5}]},
{img:"A residue read by a charm of knotted cord and iron",ent:{name:"The residue the man left",kind:"Read through a knotted charm · Register Duty-adjacent",img:"A cold weight in the ward-marks",rows:[["Register", "heavy, wrong, north-pointing"], ["Truth", "what the man left in the ward as he crossed"], ["The read", "names the seat it answers to"], ["Cost", "the charm goes cold and dead after"]]},t:["She works with a charm of knotted cord and old iron, the Grid’s kind of instrument, nothing the tower would recognise, and she puts your hand on it and makes you feel what she feels, because she says a thing this size should not be carried by one person’s word alone.", "It is a weight. North-pointing, toward water, and heavier than anything that should fit in a man, and when she reaches for the name of it the charm goes cold and dead in your joined hands and she lets go fast. A single word surfaces anyway, the way the worst words do. DUTY. “A seat,” she whispers. “He is carrying a seat of the Thirteen. God help him, and you.”"],c:[{x:"Ask the thing the Grid does not say aloud.",n:6}]},
{t:["There is a thing under all of it, the thing the unregistered whisper about and will not finish whispering, and you can reach for it or leave it. To hear it whole you would have to read her the way she read the ward, past your own careful disguise, the thing you never do."],c:[{x:"Read what the Grid is most afraid of.",lock:'clair3',n:7,do:'gridSecret'},{x:"Don’t. You have enough to carry north.",n:7,do:'gridCreditLead'}]},
{t:["You come up out of Sanya with the unregistered scattered behind you and a debt to a people who do not forget, and the Grid’s kind of truth in your hands: a sensitive’s certainty, a charm gone dead, a seat of the Thirteen riding a man going north, and a cult that fears him. No file holds any of it. No one but the Grid will ever confirm you were told.", "[ End of Chapter One, the Grid’s way. You hold the unregistered edge: a seat of the Thirteen on the move, a grief-cult that will not touch him, and a debt owed to the people who survive by being unseen. What the tower logged and sealed stays the tower’s. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]},
{t:["You tell him you will earn it, and something in him approves and does not show it. “A thing needs carrying tonight,” he says. “To someone who cannot be seen collecting it.” He gives you a word and a place and not what the thing is, because asking is its own failure down here.", "The thing is a person. You understand it on the stairwell where the handoff should happen and a young Grid runner is instead on his knees, half given over, eyes gone to someone else’s grief, and the word you were given is the only thing keeping the two people minding him from putting him down for good. The Far-Shore Circle got into him. The Grid is trying to get him out before the cult reclaims him or the tower shelves him. You walked into an extraction."],c:[{x:"Help them get him out.",n:9}]},
{img:"A working medium comes to reclaim the half-taken runner",ent:{name:"A person ridden, mid-reclaim",kind:"Far-Shore’s, half-given · Register Grief",img:"A runner with someone else’s grief in his eyes",rows:[["Register", "Grief"], ["Truth", "A Grid runner the cult is pulling under"], ["The enemy", "is the medium working the cord, not the boy"], ["Choose", "free him, or take the intel and run"]]},t:["She comes for him the way an owner comes for property, a working medium of the Circle, calm in the stairwell light, a cord of attention running from her hand to the place in the boy where his grief used to be. She does not hurry. “He came to us,” she says. “They all come to us. You can carry him out, but he will walk back in by morning, because grief is a door that only opens one way.”", "You have the word, and salt, and Gin’s cold key in your pocket, and a hard thing in front of you: the boy can be freed, but only by reaching past his grief and cutting the cord while the medium is still pulling, which is a fight you take in his place, not against his body. Or you can take what the runner already saw and get out, and leave the cord where it is."],c:[{x:"Cut the cord. Take the fight in his place.",n:10,do:'gridCultFight'},{x:"Take what he saw and run. Leave the cord.",n:11,do:'gridRun'}]},
{t:["You cut it the way you cut anything you are not strong enough to cut, by refusing to let go first, and the cord parts with a sound you feel in your teeth, and the medium loses her calm for exactly one second before she puts it back on like a coat. She does not chase. The grieving always come back; she can afford to wait. The boy comes up out of it gasping, himself, wrecked and alive.", "What he saw, he gives you while he is still shaking. The man with the wrong shadow walked through the Circle a fortnight back, and the medium who is standing right there went to her knees for him, because the thing he carried made her own master look small. He went north. Toward water. Unafraid. “The big quiet one,” the boy says. “Even the cult’s scared of him.”"],c:[{x:"Get him to safety, then go.",n:12,do:'gridFreed'}]},
{t:["You take what the runner already babbled and you go, and the cord stays in him, and you tell yourself the intel matters more than one half-taken boy you do not know, and you almost believe it. Behind you the medium does not even look up. She got what she came for. So, in a thinner way, did you.", "What the boy saw, before the grief closed back over him: the man with the wrong shadow walked through the Circle and the cult went out of his way, and he went north, toward water, carrying something that made the medium kneel. It is enough to point you. It is not enough to feel clean about."],c:[{x:"Carry it north. Don’t look back.",n:12,do:'gridRunLead'}]},
{t:["You come back to Sanya however you came back, clean or not, and Tanizaki reads which on your face before you sit. The second cup is poured. “You will do,” is all he says, and from him it is a great deal. The Grid will move the Gathering again because of tonight, because of you, and that is the shape of what you are owed and what you owe.", "[ End of Chapter One, the earned way. You hold the close, hard edge: a cult that fears the man, a seat of the Thirteen that makes mediums kneel, a runner you saved or did not, and the Grid’s slow trust paid in action. What the great houses know of a seated demon stays past a door you did not knock on. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]}
],
power:[
{img:"The cold key, and the thing you never let yourself do",t:["You have spent your whole life being a low reading on someone else’s instrument. A D. A Sensitive who finds lost keys and the mood of a room and nothing that matters. You have been so careful for so long that the carefulness has become a kind of person, and you are no longer certain where the person ends and the hiding begins.", "Tonight you stop hiding. Alone, in the flat that is too quiet, the cold key in your hand. No Directorate, no Grid, no Itsuki. Just you and the thing you have never let yourself fully do. You close your fingers around the key your brother dropped, and you reach, properly, the way you have not since you were small enough to be frightened of it. It comes. It comes so easily. Too easily, like a held breath let go."],c:[{x:"Read it. See what the key saw.",n:1}]},
{t:["You are at the edge of what you have always allowed yourself, and the edge has two sides. You can read the way a D reads, shallow and hidden, staying the small safe thing you have pretended to be, and take only the fragments that float up. Or you can drop the disguise entirely, reach the way the thing in you actually wants to, take all of it, and find out, at last, what you have been hiding from your whole life.", "The key hums against your palm. Stability is a wall, and walls come down from the inside. You can feel exactly how far you could push, and that you can feel it at all is the part you will think about later, if there is a later that recognises you."],c:[{x:"Read carefully. Stay inside the disguise.",n:2,hint:"Fragments, and safety, and the door stays closed... mostly."},{x:"Drop the disguise. Reach all the way.",n:6,hint:"Everything, at a price, and the whole hidden world turns to look."}]},
{t:["You keep yourself small, the way you always have, and read only what rises. Gin on the overpass, in the last hour anyone could call ordinary. The man near him, the shadow falling the wrong way, ahead of him, against the light. The cold. A direction, faint: north.", "And, faint as the direction, something else: far off, a thread of attention brushes the edge of even your careful reach, the way a fisher feels a touch on a long line. Something out there fishes for the gifted in the small hours, and it felt you, a little, and went still, marking the place you were."],c:[{x:"Pull the read tighter. Hold it longer.",n:3,do:'powerCareful'}]},
{t:["You hold it, carefully, and the key gives a little more. The man went north, toward water, and the weight he carried bent your careful sight the way a heavy thing bends a floor, and you let go before it could cost what it wanted to cost. You stayed a D. You stayed hidden. You got a piece, and kept your disguise, and that is the whole of the bargain.", "The far-off attention has not gone. You know its flavour now, grief and patience together, the way the grieving are gathered: a cult-thing, fishing, and it has your scent at the lowest possible volume. The Far-Shore Circle does not forget a sensitive it has felt, even faintly. You will want to remember that."],c:[{x:"Read your own reaching, the thing you never do.",lock:'clair3',n:4,do:'powerSecret'},{x:"Take the fragment and stop.",n:5,do:'powerCarefulLead'}]},
{t:["You turn the sight inward, onto your own reach, which you have never once allowed, and for a heartbeat you see the shape of the wall you have spent your life building, and what it is holding back, and how thin it actually is, and why your brother spent years making sure no one ever measured you. You put it back. Your hands are shaking. You are, technically, still a D, and you understand now that the technicality is the most fragile thing you own."],c:[{x:"Carry the fragment, and what you saw in yourself.",n:5,do:'powerCarefulLead'}]},
{t:["You come back to the too-quiet flat with a fragment and your disguise intact and a new, cold knowledge sitting behind your eyes: that you could reach further, any time, that the reaching is a door, and that things on the other side of it have begun, faintly, to wait for you to be tired enough to open it.", "[ End of Chapter One, the hidden way. You hold the careful edge: the man went north, toward water, carrying a weight that bends sight, and a grief-cult has felt you at the lowest volume and will not forget. What lies past your own wall, you chose not to look at. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]},
{img:"A second set of eyes you closed with your own hand",t:["You let go of the wall. It is not like opening your eyes; it is like finding you have always had a second set, behind the first, closed by your own hand your entire life. The key’s last hour floods you whole: the overpass, the man, the wrong shadow, the smell of a river that is not quite a river, a direction, north, and the specific gravity of the thing the man carried, a weight your new sight insists on a word for against your will.", "And the world turns to look. You feel it happen, a sweep of attention from every direction at once: a Directorate sensor somewhere logging a spike it cannot place, a Grid ward tightening three wards over, and under both, slower and vaster, something that is not an instrument at all, a regard with thirteen facets, one of which is awake. You have just made a light in a dark room full of things that hunt by light."],c:[{x:"Hold the sight. Don’t look away.",n:7,do:'powerDeep'}]},
{img:"Something arrives in the tear you made",ent:{name:"The seat that turned toward you",kind:"Drawn through a torn veil · of the Thirteen · an offer",img:"A patient enormity in the thinness",rows:[["Register", "DUTY-adjacent, and vast"], ["Truth", "a facet of the Thirteen, awake and reaching"], ["The danger", "is the offer; the offer is a seat"], ["Refuse", "with the one thing that is truly yours"]]},t:["It does not send something small. You reached too well for that. The regard comes itself, or a finger of it does, a patience the size of a throne, and it knows your name the way these things know names, by the shape of the want underneath. It shows you, because it is generous, the vacant place: a seat of the Thirteen gone empty, and the long pull of everything toward it, the Axis, the closeness that is not safety, and it shows you the man walking that pull northward, unafraid, full, and it asks if you would like to stop being so careful and so alone and so small.", "This is the trap your brother spent his life keeping you from. It would be so easy. You have the cold key in your hand, the one thing that is wholly, stubbornly, ordinarily yours."],c:[{x:"Refuse it. Close your hand on the key and push it out.",n:8,do:'powerFight'},{x:"Pull back before it finishes the offer.",n:9,do:'powerPullLead'}]},
{t:["You refuse it the way you have refused yourself for years, which is the one thing you are genuinely good at, your fist closed white around a cheap brass key, and you force the tear shut around the regard, and it withdraws with something that is almost amusement and entirely patient. It will be back. They always come back to the ones who can reach.", "But you held the sight to the end, and you kept what it showed you, and it is more than anyone else on any other road will have. The man carries a seat of the Thirteen, of the DUTY register, and he is walking the Axis-pull north, toward the empty throne, toward water, unafraid, because for a seated one there is nothing left to fear. And you know how it is done, now, because for one moment the same door stood open in you, and the same offer was made, and you understand that he was not taken. He was reached, at his hardest reach, for someone he loved."],c:[{x:"Write it down with shaking hands.",n:9,do:'powerDeepLead'}]},
{t:["You come back to yourself owing debts you did not have this morning. One to the veil, which has your full scent now, not the careful volume but all of it, and which knows you can reach, and will keep offering. One to the Thirteen, one facet of which has looked at you and found you interesting, which is the worst thing you could possibly be to it. One to Gin, who came no nearer to being found, except that you understand him better than anyone alive, because for one moment you stood exactly where he stood and were offered exactly what he was offered, reaching for someone you love.", "[ End of Chapter One, the open-door way. You hold the deepest, most dangerous edge: the Axis, the empty seat, the offer itself, the truth that he was reached and not taken. And the whole hidden world has your face now. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]}
],
look:[
{img:"Ōji at four in the morning, a held breath",t:["You do not call anyone. You do not open the book, or reach for the gift, or knock on any door. You put on your shoes and go out into the four-in-the-morning city and let it have you, the way Gin used to say the long way finds what the short ways miss. You used to think it was just something he said.", "Ōji at this hour is a held breath. Shuttered shops, a vending machine humming its one note, a cat crossing the road like it holds the lease. You walk without choosing a direction and find you have been choosing one all along, the way you always do. The city is not empty. It only looks empty to people who are not paying attention, and you have spent your whole life paying attention and pretending not to."],c:[{x:"Keep walking. Let the city decide.",n:1}]},
{t:["The walk forks the way walks do, not at a sign but at a feeling. One way the streets get warmer, a thread of light and noise from the places that stay open for the people who cannot sleep, the bars and the stands where the city keeps its insomniacs and its secrets. The other way the streets go quiet and cold and downhill, toward the water, toward the riverbank where, your grandmother used to say, the dead come home.", "Both are true at this hour. The city holds both. But it is Obon, the week the doors between here and there stand open, and tonight one of those two ways is louder than it has any right to be, and you cannot yet tell which."],c:[{x:"Toward the lit places, the people still awake.",n:2,hint:"The night people see everything and forget on purpose."},{x:"Toward the empty places, and the river.",n:6,hint:"Obon, and the dead coming home, and what disturbed them."}]},
{img:"The Suzuran, nine seats and a held match",t:["The Suzuran is nine seats and a bartender and a light the colour of a held match. Kaneda is polishing a glass that is already clean, the way men do when the real work is the listening. He does not know you, sizes you up in the time it takes to set the glass down, slides a small one across. “First one’s on the house. You look like the kind of trouble that pays for itself later.”", "You are straight with him, and he pours himself one, which he does not do for liars, and you are three sentences in when it happens. A regular at the end of the bar, an old man who has been crying quietly into the same drink for an hour, stands up wrong. Not drunk. Wrong, the way a room goes wrong. His grief is not his anymore; something is wearing it, and it has been working him slow all week, here, in the warm bright place where the lonely come, and tonight it is ready to take him home."],c:[{x:"Help him. Don’t let the bright place be a trap.",n:3,do:'lookPeople'}]},
{t:["Kaneda is already moving, salt from under the bar in his fist, because a man who pours for the night crowd has seen this before and knows what it is: the Far-Shore Circle does not only fish the riverbank. It fishes the warm rooms too, the bars and the all-night counters, anywhere the grieving gather and feel safe enough to put their guard down. You and Kaneda get the old man’s grief back into his own hands between you, salt and a steady voice and the cold key in your pocket, and he sits down hard and weeps, himself again, which is more than the thing offered him.", "Kaneda pours you a real one, after. “That,” he says, “is the third this month. Somebody is hungry in this ward.” And then, low, the thing the city has been not-saying: “There’s a man been walking nights. Cameras out. Shadow gets there before he does. People who see him won’t say what was wrong, only that something was. If I were you, I’d walk north. Toward the water. That’s the direction the not-saying points.”"],c:[{x:"Read the ward through Kaneda, the way you never do.",lock:'clair3',n:4,do:'lookSecret'},{x:"Take the rumor and go.",n:5,do:'lookPeopleLead'}]},
{t:["You let yourself read him, lightly, the bartender and the bar and the ward sitting behind it, the way you never do because reading the living is the line you do not cross. Under Kaneda’s plain steadiness the ward is a held breath, and you feel why: the whole district has been thinning for weeks, a slow tide going out, and the cult is only feeding harder because the feeding has gotten easier, because something far bigger is pulling the water of the world toward an empty place, and the small predators are gorging in the shallows it leaves behind."],c:[{x:"Carry the rumor, and what you felt under it.",n:5,do:'lookPeopleLead'}]},
{t:["You walk back out into the small hours owing the lightest of debts, a drink and a shared bad minute with a man who will forget you on purpose. You have the warm-rooms truth: a cult feeding harder than it should, a ward going quietly thin, an old man saved, and a direction the not-saying points. North. The water.", "[ End of Chapter One, the lit way. You hold the human edge: the Far-Shore feeding in the warm places, the ward thinning toward something, the man who walks nights going north. What the river holds, and what the dead saw of him, you walked away from. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]},
{img:"The riverbank at Obon, the dead come home wrong",t:["You go down toward the water, where the city runs out of reasons to be loud. The riverbank at four in the morning is the oldest thing in Tokyo, older than the towers, older than the Directorate. Your grandmother brought you here once, at Obon, to set a paper lantern on the current for people you were too young to have lost. The dead come home along the water, she said, and you never quite stopped half-believing it.", "Tonight you do not have to half-believe it. The dead are home, and they are not at peace. The whole reach of the river is wrong, the membrane worn to almost nothing, lanterns from a hundred grieving families guttering in a wind that is not there, and the returning dead are agitated, crowding the waterline, all of them turned the same way, north, the way animals turn from a fire. Something crossed here, going north, and it frightened the dead, and the dead do not frighten easily."],c:[{x:"Walk the waterline. See what crossed.",n:7}]},
{img:"A medium working the mourners at the waterline",ent:{name:"A mourner the Circle is taking",kind:"Far-Shore’s, at the Obon grief · Register Grief",img:"A kneeling figure with borrowed sorrow",rows:[["Register", "Grief"], ["Truth", "A grieving family member, drawn down at the water"], ["The enemy", "is the medium working the lantern-light, not the mourner"], ["Free her", "reach past the sorrow with what is yours"]]},t:["The crossing left a witness, the kind the water keeps, a residue caught at the edge of returning, and it would tell you what it saw, except that you cannot get to it, because a working medium of the Far-Shore Circle is between you and the water, mid-rite, harvesting the Obon grief the way you harvest a field that has done your work for you. A mourner kneels at the lantern-light with someone else’s sorrow climbing into her, and the medium does not even look up. “Everyone comes to the water to put a grief down,” she says. “She came to put hers down. So did you.”", "You have salt, and Gin’s cold key, and the dead at your back all turned north. The mourner is the one in danger; the medium is the rite. You can break it and free her, or step back and let the dead witness tell you what it saw, and not everyone gets to do both before the lanterns go out."],c:[{x:"Free the mourner. Break the rite with what is yours.",n:8,do:'lookFight'},{x:"Step back and let the dead show you what they saw.",n:9,do:'lookRiverLead'}]},
{t:["You break it the way you break anything you are not strong enough to break, by refusing to let go first, salt and a steady hand and a cheap brass key, and the borrowed sorrow comes off the mourner all at once and she folds down around her own, which is hers, survivable. The medium loses her patience for exactly one second, then puts it back on like a coat, and withdraws into the lantern-dark. The grieving always come back. She can wait.", "And now the dead will let you near, because you did a kind thing at their water. The witness gives up what it saw the way the dead give anything, gently. The man with the wrong shadow crossed here going north, and the dead all turned from him, because what he carried was not a passenger but a throne, a seat of the Thirteen, of the DUTY register, and it was walking the long pull north toward an empty place, and he was not afraid, and the dead know there is only one kind of thing that walks among them unafraid."],c:[{x:"Set a lantern for him. Then go.",n:9,do:'lookRiverLead'}]},
{t:["You set a paper lantern on the current the way your grandmother taught you, for a man who is not dead and may be worse, and you watch it join the others going wrong in the windless dark, and you walk back up from the water carrying the heaviest truth of all the truths you could have carried this morning, and the loneliest.", "[ End of Chapter One, the water’s way. You hold the oldest edge: a seat of the Thirteen on the move, the dead themselves turning from it, a cult gorging in the shallows of a world being pulled toward an empty place, and your brother walking north into all of it, unafraid. The city handed it to you because you walked slow enough, and at the water, to be given it. Chapter Two is being written. ]"],c:[{x:"Start the morning over",scene:'opening',n:0,do:'reset'}]}
]
});
